  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Desinencias del presente en -ere",
    "@en": "The present in -ere"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Los verbos en **-ere** usan las siguientes terminaciones: **io -o**, **tu -i**, **lui/lei/Lei -e**, **noi -iamo**, **voi -ete**, **loro -ono**.",
     "@en": "**-ere** verbs use the following endings: **io -o**, **tu -i**, **lui/lei/Lei -e**, **noi -iamo**, **voi -ete**, **loro -ono**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Atención a las diferencias con -are: la tercera persona singular acaba en **-e** (**lui prende**, **lei scrive**; no *-a*). La segunda plural termina en **-ete** (**voi prendete**). Y en tercera plural termina en **-ono**, con acento esdrújulo en la raíz: **PREN-do-no**, **SCRÍ-vo-no**, **VÉ-do-no**.",
     "@en": "Attention to differences with -are: the third person singular ends in **-e** (**lui prende**, **lei scrive**; no * -a *). The second plural ends in **-ete** (**voi prendete**). And in the third plural it ends in **-ono**, with an emphasis on the root: **PREN-do-no**, **SCRÍ-vo-no**, **VÉ-do-no**."
    }
   ]
  },
